# AWS CLI Log Sync

## Process

- Configured AWS CLI for authenticated access to the AWS environment
- Used `aws s3 sync` to recursively download CloudTrail logs from Amazon S3
- Created a reusable shell script to simplify bulk log retrieval
- Stored downloaded logs locally for Splunk ingestion and analysis

## Result

Automated the collection of AWS CloudTrail logs from S3 instead of manually downloading individual files.

## Insight

Using AWS CLI for log retrieval is more efficient and scalable than manual downloads.

This adds a cloud engineering component to the project and makes the logging workflow more realistic for production-style environments.
